<section class="block" id="compare">
  <div class="wrap grid">
    <h2>Compared with caffeinate, Amphetamine and pmset</h2>
    <div class="text">
      <p>caffeinate and Amphetamine create power assertions. macOS honors those while the lid is open, but not when you close the lid on battery. Only <code>pmset -a disablesleep 1</code> does that.</p>
      <p>You can run it by hand, and it works. Then nothing watches the temperature, the charge or the network, and it stays on until you undo it with <code>sudo pmset -a disablesleep 0</code>.</p>
      <p>StayAwake runs the same command through a small root helper and adds the rules above and a fail-safe that restores sleep if the app dies. If you only need the Mac awake with the lid open, caffeinate or Amphetamine are the simpler tool.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
